# HG changeset patch
# Martin F. Schumann <github@mfs.name> and Kilo Code
# Date 1793040818 +0100
Feature: Linux systray: Restore maximized state when starting minimized to tray.

On Wayland a window that is hidden before it has ever been mapped never
receives a window-state-event, so gtk_window_is_maximized() reports false
even though the XUL window's sizemode attribute says "maximized". In that
case restoreGeometry() unmaximized the window and resized it to the default
geometry, which is why starting minimized to the tray produced a tiny window
instead of a maximized one (Issue #627).

